File No. 14X002
Security Agreement, Page 1

BUSINESS READY COMMUNITY – BUSINESS COMMITTED
LOAN AND SECURITY AGREEMENT

This BUSINESS READY COMMUNITY – BUSINESS COMMITTED LOAN AND SECURITY
AGREEMENT (this “Agreement”) is made as of the _______ day of _______________, 2014,
between CITY OF CHEYENNE, a Wyoming municipal corporation, whose principal office and
mailing address is located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, WY 82001 (the “City”), and
WYOMING BUSINESS COUNCIL (the “Council”), a body corporate organized under the laws
of the State of Wyoming and operating as a state instrumentality operated solely for the
public benefit, whose principal office and mailing address is located at 214 West 15th Street,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
Explanatory Statement
A. City has made a loan to Granite Peak Development Limited Partnership, a Wyoming
limited partnership formerly known as Granite Peak Development, LLC, a Wyoming
Limited Liability Company (“Granite”), in the stated principal sum of $3,000,000 (the
“Granite Loan”), as evidenced by a Non-Negotiable Promissory Note dated as of even
date made by Granite and the City and guarantied by Rich Fairservis (the “Guarantor”),
all in connection with the project (the “Project”) to construct railways, spurs, and
switching and related facilities to serve the Swan Ranch Rail Park (the “Park”) in
Cheyenne, Wyoming.
B. The City, the Cheyenne-Laramie County Corporation for Economic Development
(Cheyenne Leads), a Wyoming non-profit corporation and statutorily-authorized
community development organization ("LEADS"), and Granite will construct the Project
in accordance with an undated Amended and Restated Project Development and
Administration Agreement (the “Development Agreement”) made among them.
C. During construction and afterward during the pendency of the Granite Loan, the City will
own the project improvements pursuant to an Assignment of Ownership of Rail, Ties,
and all Related Rail Equipment (the “Rail Ownership Assignment”) installed pursuant to
Amended And Restated Project Development and Administration Agreement dated as of
even date herewith.
D. Pursuant to a Rail Road Right of Way Easement made as of even date herewith and
recorded on ______________, 2014, in Book _____ at Page _____ among the Real
Estate Records of the County Clerk for Laramie County, Wyoming (the “Rail Easement
Agreement”), made by Swan Ranch, LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company
(“Swan”), and Clear Creek Land Company LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company
(“Clear Creek”), the City will be the owner, for a term of ten (10) years from the date
hereof, of a non-exclusive easement (the “Rail Easement”) for a rail road line and
corridor in Parcels 2, 3, and 4, as described and shown on Exhibits A, B, and C to
Schedule 1 hereof, which schedule and exhibits are incorporated herein by this reference,
subject to the rights of Granite, Swan, CLH, LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company
(“CLH”), and any related entity to an exclusive option to acquire the rail, ties, and all
related rail equipment installed pursuant to the Development Agreement and all of the
City’s right, title, and interest in the Rail Easement.
```

### Page 2 of 17

```text
File No. 14X002
Security Agreement, Page 2

E. The City has entered into a Track Lease Agreement for Rail Facilities Within Swan
Ranch Rail Park, Cheyenne, Wyoming (the “Track Lease Agreement”), with CLH and
Granite under which CLH will lease the City's rail facilities within the Park to serve
various business enterprises now or to be located within the Park.
F. The City has applied for, and been approved by the Council for, a Wyoming Business
Ready Community-Business Committed Loan in the maximum principal sum of Three
Million Dollars ($3,000,000) (the “Loan”).  The City of Cheyenne will distribute the
proceeds of the Loan to Granite pursuant to the terms of the Development Agreement,
among other documents, which proceeds are required to be used exclusively to fund a
portion of the costs of construction of the Project.
G. The Granite Note is secured, in part, by a Mortgage (the “Mortgage”) upon the lands
described as Parcel 1 on Schedule 1 hereto granted to the City by Swan and Clear Creek.
H. The City’s obligations to repay the Loan to the Council is evidenced by a Promissory
Note (the “Note”) of even date herewith made in the maximum principal sum of the
Loan.
I. As collateral security for the City’s obligations under the Note, this Agreement, and the
other Loan Documents, the City, and others, have entered into the following instruments:
1) a Collateral Assignment of Note and Mortgage, wherein the City has assigned all of
its interest in and to the Granite Note and the Mortgage to the Council;
2) a Collateral Assignment of Railroad Easement and Track Lease, wherein the City has
assigned all of its interest in and to the Rail Easement Agreement and the Track Lease
Agreement to the Council;
J. Under the terms of this Agreement, the Council desires to establish the terms and
conditions upon which it will loan the Loan Proceeds to the City in periodic advances as
construction progresses, and to additionally secure its performance of the Loan, the City
desires to grant to the Council a security interest in and to all of the Collateral (defined
below).
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the Explanatory Statement (which is a
substantive part hereof) and other good and valuable consideration, the City, intending to be
legally bound, agrees as follows:
1. Definitions.
1.1. “Collateral” shall include all of the City’s interest in and to the personal property
described on Schedule 2 attached hereto and made a part hereof by this reference.
1.2. “Collateral Assignments” means the Collateral Assignment described in Paragraph I
of the Explanatory Statement.
1.3. “Loan Documents” means the Note (as defined above), the Collateral Assignments,
this Agreement, and all other documents, certificate, instruments, applications, opinions, and
other writings evidencing, securing, executed, or otherwise made or delivered in connection with
the Loan.
```

