8.4. No advance shall be made for any services or materials provided in connection with
the Project before the date on which the last required signature is affixed to this Agreement.
8.5. If the actual costs of the Project exceed the available funds indicated in Attachment
B to the Grant Agreement, the City will have no obligation to pay for any additional cost of the
Project.
8.6. If there is additional funding required to complete the Project, the City must provide
to the Council all necessary information regarding the funding.
8.7. The City will be required to provide a letter from a qualified engineer certifying the
construction completion of the Project and that all required construction standards were adhered
to during the construction of the Project.  The City will be required to provide information as
requested by the Council about lease arrangements, job creation, additional investments,
marketing, business recruitment, and business development efforts.  All promotional and
marketing information and materials created for the Project will be required to reference the
Council as a funding partner.  The City will cause Granite to provide all information necessary to
it to facilitate the City’s compliance with these requirements.
9. Events of Default.  The City shall, at the Council’s option, be in default under this
Agreement upon the happening of any of the following events or conditions (each, an “Event of
Default”):
9.1. a failure to pay any amount due under the Note or any Loan Document when due;
9.2. a failure by the City to perform any of its other obligations under the Grant
Agreement;
9.3. the failure by the City to perform any of its other obligations under this Agreement
or any other Loan Document within thirty (30) days of notice from Council of the same;
9.4. material falsity, inaccuracy or breach by the City of any written warranty,
representation or statement made or furnished to the Council by or on behalf of the City;
9.5. an uninsured material loss, theft, damage, or destruction to any of the Collateral, or
the entry of any judgment against the City or any lien against or the making of any levy upon,
seizure of or attachment relating to the Collateral;
9.6. the failure of the Council to have at all times during which the Loan is outstanding, a
perfected first priority security interest in the Collateral; or
9.7. the City becomes insolvent; or admits in writing its inability to pay its debts as they
mature; or applies for, consents to or acquiesces in the appointment of a trustee, receiver or
custodian for it or a substantial part of its property; or, in the absence of such application,
consent or acquiescence, a trustee, receiver or custodian is appointed for the City or a substantial
part of its property and is not discharged within sixty (60) days; or any bankruptcy,
