### Page 6 of 17

```text
File No. 14X002
Security Agreement, Page 6

reorganization, debt arrangement, moratorium, or any proceeding under any bankruptcy or
insolvency law, or any dissolution or liquidation proceeding is instituted by or against the City
and, if instituted against the City, is consented to or acquiesced in by the City or is not dismissed
within sixty (60) days.
10. Remedies.
10.1. Upon the occurrence of any Event of Default and at any time thereafter, the
Council may declare all Obligations secured hereby immediately due and payable and shall have,
in addition to any remedies provided herein or by any applicable law or in equity, all the
remedies of a secured party under the UCC.
10.2. The Council’s remedies include, but are not limited to, to the extent permitted by
law, the right to (a) peaceably by its own means or with judicial assistance enter the City’s
premises and take possession of the Collateral without prior notice to the City or the opportunity
for a hearing, (b) render the Collateral unusable, (c) dispose of the Collateral on the City’s
premises, and (d) require the City to assemble the Collateral and make it available to the Council
at a place designated by the Council.
10.3. Unless the Collateral is perishable or threatens to decline speedily in value or is of
a type customarily sold on a recognized market, the Council will give the City reasonable notice
of the time and place of any public sale thereof or of the time after which any private sale or any
other intended disposition thereof is to be made.  The requirements of commercially reasonable
notice shall be met if such notice is sent to the City at least five (5) days before the time of the
intended sale or disposition.  Expenses of retaking, holding, preparing for sale, selling or the like
shall include the Council’s reasonable attorney’s fees and legal expenses, incurred or expended
by the Council to enforce any payment due it under the Loan Documents either as against the
City, or in the prosecution or defense of any action, or concerning any matter growing out of or
connection with the Loan and the Collateral pledged hereunder.
10.4. The City waives all relief from all appraisement or exemption laws now in force
or hereafter enacted.
11. Payment of Expenses.  At its option, the Council may, but is not required to:  discharge
taxes, liens, security interests or such other encumbrances as may attach to the Collateral; pay for
required insurance on the Collateral; and pay for the maintenance, appraisal or reappraisal, and
preservation of the Collateral, as determined by the Council to be necessary.  The City will
reimburse the Council on demand for any payment so made or any expense incurred by the
Council pursuant to the foregoing authorization, and the Collateral also will secure any advances
or payments so made or expenses so incurred by the Council.
12. Notices.  All notices, demands, requests, consents, approvals and other communications
required or permitted hereunder must be in writing and will be effective upon receipt.  Such
notices and other communications may be delivered as provided in the Note.
13. Preservation of Rights.  No delay or omission on the Council’s part to exercise any right
or power arising hereunder will impair any such right or power or be considered a waiver of any
such right or power, nor will the Council’s action or inaction impair any such right or power.
```

### Page 7 of 17

```text
File No. 14X002
Security Agreement, Page 7

The Council’s rights and remedies hereunder are cumulative and not exclusive of any other
rights or remedies which the Council may have under other agreements, at law or in equity.
14. General Provisions.
14.1. Severability.  In case any one or more of the provisions contained in this
Agreement should be invalid, illegal or unenforceable in any respect, the validity, legality and
enforceability of the remaining provisions contained herein shall not in any way be affected or
impaired thereby.
14.2. Amendments. Any changes, modifications, revisions, or amendments to the Loan
which are mutually agreed upon by the parties to the Loan shall be incorporated by written
instrument, executed and signed by all parties to the Loan.
14.3. Entire Agreement.  This Agreement (including the documents and instruments
referred to herein) constitutes the entire agreement and supersedes all other prior agreements and
understandings, both written and oral, between the parties with respect to the subject matter
hereof.
14.4. Counterparts.  This Agreement may be signed in any number of counterpart
copies and by the parties hereto on separate counterparts, but all such copies shall constitute one
and the same instrument.  Delivery of an executed counterpart of a signature page to this
Agreement by facsimile transmission shall be effective as delivery of a manually executed
counterpart.  Any party so executing this Agreement by facsimile transmission shall promptly
deliver a manually executed counterpart, provided that any failure to do so shall not affect the
validity of the counterpart executed by facsimile transmission.  The term “facsimile
transmission” shall include images of documents sent by email.
14.5. Successors and Assigns.  This Agreement will be binding upon and inure to the
benefit of the City and the Council and their respective heirs, executors, administrators,
successors and assigns; provided, however, that the City may not assign this Agreement in whole
or in part without the Council’s prior written consent and the Council at any time may assign this
Agreement in whole or in part.
14.6. Interpretation.  In this Agreement, unless the Council and the City otherwise
agree in writing, the singular includes the plural and the plural the singular; words importing any
gender include the other genders; references to statutes are to be construed as including all
statutory provisions consolidating, amending or replacing the statute referred to; the word “or”
shall be deemed to include “and/or”, the words “including”, “includes” and “include” shall be
deemed to be followed by the words “without limitation”; references to articles, sections (or
subdivisions of sections) or exhibits are to those of this Agreement unless otherwise indicated.
Section headings in this Agreement are included for convenience of reference only and shall not
constitute a part of this Agreement for any other purpose.  If this Agreement is executed by more
than one City, the obligations of such persons or entities will be joint and several.
14.7. Governing Law; Jurisdiction; Venue.  This Agreement has been delivered to and
accepted by the Council and will be deemed to be made in the State of Wyoming.  The City
hereby irrevocably consents to the exclusive jurisdiction of any state or federal court in Laramie
County, Wyoming; provided that nothing contained in this Agreement will prevent the Council
```

### Page 8 of 17

```text
File No. 14X002
Security Agreement, Page 8

from bringing any action, enforcing any award or judgment or exercising any rights against the
City individually or against any security pledged by Granite located within any other county,
state or other foreign or domestic jurisdiction.  The Courts of the State of Wyoming shall have
jurisdiction over the Loan and the parties, and the venue shall be the First Judicial District,
Laramie County, Wyoming.  The City waives any objection to venue and any objection based on
a more convenient forum in any action instituted under this Agreement.
14.8. Monitoring Activities.  The Council shall have the right to monitor all Loan
related activities of the City and all Guarantors.  This shall include, but not be limited to, the
right to make site inspections at any time, to bring experts and consultants on site to examine or
evaluate completed work or work in progress, and to observe all City personnel in every phase of
performance of Loan related work.
14.9. No Finder’s Fees.  No finder’s fee, real estate commission, or other similar fee or
charge related to the procurement of the Loan shall be paid by either party.
14.10. Audit/Access to Records.  The Council and its representatives shall have access to
any books, documents, papers, electronic data and records of the City which are pertinent to the
Loan.  The City shall immediately, upon receiving written instruction from the Council, provide
to any independent auditor or accountant all books, documents, papers, electronic data and
records of the City which are pertinent to the Loan.  The City shall cooperate fully with any such
independent auditor or accountant during the entire course of any audit authorized by the
Council.
14.11. Availability of Funds; Subject to Appropriation; Agreement to Pursue
Appropriations; No General Obligation.  Each payment obligation of the Council is conditioned
upon the availability of government funds which are appropriated or allocated for the payment of
this obligation.  If funds are not allocated and available for continued performance of the Loan,
the Loan may be terminated by the Council at the end of the period for which the funds are
available.  The Council shall notify the City at the earliest possible time of the services which
will or may be affected by a shortage of funds.  No penalty shall accrue to the Council in the
event this provision is exercised, and the Council shall not be obligated or liable for any future
payments due or for any damages as a result of termination under this section.  This provision
shall not be construed to permit the Council to terminate the Loan to acquire similar services
from another party.  In addition, the Council agrees, to the extent within its power and authority,
to take all necessary steps and make timely requests for the appropriation of funds to fund and
maintain all advances under the Loan and to use its reasonable efforts to cause such
appropriations to be made.  Under no circumstances shall the Council’s obligations to fund the
Loan be deemed, considered, interpreted, or construed to be a general obligation of the Council.
14.12. Certificate of Good Standing.  The City shall provide to the Council a certificate
of good standing, verifying compliance with the unemployment insurance and workers’
compensation programs at all times the Loan is outstanding, as applicable.
14.13. Compliance with Laws.  The City shall keep informed of and comply with all
applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations in the performance of its operations.
14.14. Ethics.  City shall keep informed of and comply with the Wyoming Ethics and
Disclosure Act (Wyo. Stat. § 9-13-101, et seq.), to the extent applicable to it and/or the Loan.
