14.23. Third Party Beneficiary Rights.  The parties do not intend to create in any other
individual or entity the status of third party beneficiary, and the Loan shall not be construed so as
to create such status.  The rights, duties, and obligations under the Loan shall operate only
between the City and the Council and shall inure solely to the benefit of them.
14.24. Time is of the Essence.  Time is of the essence in all provisions of the Loan.
14.25. Titles Not Controlling.  Titles of sections and subsections are for reference only
and shall not be used to construe the actual language of the applicable provisions.
14.26. Waiver.  The waiver of any breach of any term or condition in the Loan shall not
be deemed a waiver of any prior or subsequent breach. Failure to object to a breach shall not
constitute a waiver.
15. WAIVER OF JURY TRIAL.  EACH OF THE CITY AND THE COUNCIL
IRREVOCABLY WAIVES ANY AND ALL RIGHT IT MAY HAVE TO A TRIAL BY
JURY IN ANY ACTION, PROCEEDING OR CLAIM OF ANY NATURE RELATING
TO THIS AGREEMENT, ANY DOCUMENTS EXECUTED IN CONNECTION WITH
THIS AGREEMENT OR ANY TRANSACTION CONTEMPLATED IN ANY OF SUCH
DOCUMENTS.  THE CITY AND THE COUNCIL ACKNOWLEDGE THAT THE
FOREGOING WAIVER IS KNOWING AND VOLUNTARY AND MADE AFTER
AMPLE OPPORTUNITY TO CONSULT WITH THEIR RESPECTIVE LEGAL
ADVISORS.
16. Non-General Obligation.  This Agreement is for a loan from the Wyoming Business
Council to the City of Cheyenne, as described below and in the identified attachments thereto.
This Agreement and the any and all attachments thereto will not encumber, be chargeable,
create or constitute a legal or moral obligation or debt of any kind on behalf of or against the
City of Cheyenne and will not encumber or be chargeable against, the City’s assets, general
reserves, general funds, obligation funds, or any other revenues or properties whatsoever.

Without limiting the generality of the provisions of this Section, neither this
Agreement nor any of the Loan Documents (i) shall result in the imposition of any debt
upon the City in contravention of any constitutional or statutory limitations or
requirements concerning the indebtedness of the City; (ii) shall constitute a pledge of or
result in the imposition of any lien, charge or encumbrance upon any tax revenues, cash
reserves, or other assets or revenues of the City; or (iii) shall, in the event of a default
hereunder or thereunder, entitle the Council to, and the Council shall not have, the right to
seek repayment of the principal or accrued interest due under the Loan, or any other sums
payable under the Loan, from any source other than the collateral now or hereafter
pledged by Granite or its affiliates to the City to secure the indebtedness contemplated by
the Development Agreement.
IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the City has caused this Agreement to be executed by its Mayor
and attested by it City Clerk, all as of the date first written above.
ATTEST:
CITY OF CHEYENNE
```

